  Rendered by iarch/cli/render_gtk_css.py into ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css.

  GTK 3 is not GTK 4 with the serial number filed off, and this sheet is written
  against what {{ verified.gtk3 }} actually parses, per data/design/gtk.json:

  * no backdrop-filter and no filter at all, so the frosted look here is a
    translucent background-color and the blur the compositor applies through the
    window rules in .config/hypr/generated/glass.lua, not a filter in this file;
  * no transform, so a pressed button gets a darker fill instead of a scale;
  * no @media, so there is no prefers-reduced-motion query to answer; durations
    come from the intensity, and the Performance intensity sets them low;
  * :focus-visible does not exist, so the focus ring hangs off :focus;
  * :hover and :disabled exist as aliases, but :prelight and :insensitive are
    the spellings older themes use, so both are listed;
  * menu and menuitem are the real nodes here, where GTK 4 uses popover and
    modelbutton.

  GTK CSS has no !important at either version, so this file wins on cascade
  order: it is parsed after the theme.
-#}
{%- macro alpha(color, value) -%}alpha({{ color }}, {{ value }}){%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro ring(width) -%}
  outline-color: {{ alpha(c.accent, 0.55) }};
  outline-style: solid;
  outline-width: {{ width }}px;
  outline-offset: -{{ width }}px;
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro transition(props, duration, easing) -%}
  transition-property: {{ props }};
  transition-duration: {{ duration }}ms;
  transition-timing-function: {{ easing }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro shadow(y, blur, alpha_value) -%}0 {{ y }}px {{ blur }}px {{ alpha(c.shadow, alpha_value) }}{%- endmacro -%}

/* ---- the roles this sheet uses, defined once ---------------------------- */
@define-color iarch_accent {{ c.accent }};
@define-color iarch_on_accent {{ c.on_accent }};
@define-color iarch_surface {{ c.surface }};
